module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Subsheaf
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoproductInclusion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Glueing.SheafCoproduct
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.PointsAndCoverings.Retrofit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Representable

/-!
# Summands of a coproduct of sheaves: clopen inclusions and algebraicity

A coproduct of sheaves of sets, over an index type of any size, splits as the binary
coproduct of any one of its summands and "the rest": the subsheaf generated by the images of
the other summands. Combined with Stacks 0F15 for binary coproducts this says that on the
big fppf site of `S` *every* coproduct inclusion `F i ⟶ ∐ F` is representable by open
immersions, and also by closed immersions; and since a representable transformation into an
algebraic space has an algebraic space as its source, every summand of a coproduct which is
an algebraic space over `S` is again an algebraic space over `S` (Stacks 02WP).

The clopen half is the input through which the diagonal of a coproduct of algebraic spaces is
analysed: a section of `∐ F i` over a scheme `T` of the site decomposes `T` into the
pairwise-disjoint clopen pieces on which it comes from one summand.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductComplement` is "the rest" of a coproduct after removing one
  summand, with `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductComplementSubfunctor` the subfunctor it
  sheafifies and `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductComplementIncl` its inclusion.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isColimit_binaryCofan_coproductComplement`: a coproduct of sheaves is
  the binary coproduct of any summand and the subsheaf generated by the other summands.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductIncl_isOpenImmersion` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductIncl_isClosedImmersion`: **Stacks 0F15** for a coproduct over
  an arbitrary index type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_of_coproduct`: **Stacks 02WP**, algebraicity of
  each summand.

## Implementation notes

"The rest" is `AlgebraicGeometry.coproductComplement`: the sheafification, in the sense of
`CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.sheafify`, of the supremum of the ranges of the other coproduct
inclusions. Sheafifying the subfunctor is what makes it a sheaf without assuming that the
site admits sheafification, and the universal property is checked against it with
`CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.to_sheafify_lift_unique`: two morphisms out of the sheafified
subfunctor agree as soon as they agree on the subfunctor itself.

The splitting and its supporting constructions are stated for an arbitrary Grothendieck
topology on a category with objects in `Type (u+1)` and morphisms in `Type u`, since nothing
about schemes is used; the application to the big fppf site is the arbitrary-index form of
Stacks 0F15 that follows it.

The tag `0F15` is not attached here: the tagged statement is the binary one, proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoproductInclusion.lean`, and these are its
arbitrary-index corollaries.

Stacks 02WP is stated through the universal property of a colimit cocone rather than through
a chosen coproduct and an isomorphism, so that it retains the source's statement without
choosing a model for the coproduct. At a fixed index the coproduct cofan splits as a binary
coproduct of that summand and the sheaf generated by the others
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.splitColimit`), so the inclusion of the summand is one half of a
binary coproduct and is therefore representable by open immersions. That splitting and the
one used for Stacks 0F15 above are two independent constructions of "the rest" of a
coproduct, built out of different infrastructure; neither statement is phrased in terms of
the other.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F15](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F15)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02WP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02WP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02WQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02WQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

section General

variable {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {I : Type v}

/-- The subfunctor of a presheaf generated by the images of a family of morphisms into it,
omitting the `i`-th member. -/
noncomputable def coproductComplementSubfunctor {Fi : I → Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}
    (f : ∀ j, Fi j ⟶ F) (i : I) : Subfunctor F :=
  ⨆ j : {j : I // j ≠ i}, Subfunctor.range (f j.1)

/-- "The rest" of a coproduct of sheaves after removing the `i`-th summand: the subsheaf of
the coproduct generated by the images of the other summands. -/
noncomputable def coproductComplement {Fi : I → Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {F : Sheaf J (Type u)}
    (f : ∀ j, Fi j ⟶ F.obj) (i : I) : Sheaf J (Type u) :=
  ⟨((coproductComplementSubfunctor f i).sheafify J).toFunctor,
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).mpr
      ((coproductComplementSubfunctor f i).sheafify_isSheaf
        ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).mp F.property))⟩

/-- The inclusion into the coproduct of "the rest" of a coproduct of sheaves. -/
noncomputable def coproductComplementIncl {Fi : I → Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {F : Sheaf J (Type u)}
    (f : ∀ j, Fi j ⟶ F.obj) (i : I) : coproductComplement f i ⟶ F :=
  ⟨Subfunctor.ι ((coproductComplementSubfunctor f i).sheafify J)⟩

/-- A coproduct of sheaves of sets is the binary coproduct of any one of its summands and
the subsheaf generated by the images of the other summands. -/
noncomputable def isColimit_binaryCofan_coproductComplement
    {Fi : I → Sheaf J (Type u)} {F : Sheaf J (Type u)} (f : ∀ i, Fi i ⟶ F)
    (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk F f)) (i : I) :
    IsColimit (BinaryCofan.mk (f i)
      (coproductComplementIncl (J := J) (fun j => (f j).hom) i)) := by
  classical
  let T := coproductComplementSubfunctor (fun j => (f j).hom) i
  let G := coproductComplement (J := J) (fun j => (f j).hom) i
  let k := coproductComplementIncl (J := J) (fun j => (f j).hom) i
  have hTle (j : I) (hj : j ≠ i) : Subfunctor.range (f j).hom ≤ T := by
    intro V x hx
    change x ∈ (⨆ j : {j : I // j ≠ i}, Subfunctor.range (f j.1).hom).obj V
    rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj]
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨⟨j, hj⟩, hx⟩
  let gj (j : I) (hj : j ≠ i) : Fi j ⟶ G :=
    { hom := Subfunctor.lift (f j).hom ((hTle j hj).trans (Subfunctor.le_sheafify J T)) }
  have hfacG (j : I) (hj : j ≠ i) : gj j hj ≫ k = f j := by
    apply Sheaf.hom_ext
    ext V x
    rfl
  let d (X : Sheaf J (Type u)) (a : Fi i ⟶ X) (b : G ⟶ X) : F ⟶ X :=
    Cofan.IsColimit.desc hc fun j =>
      if hj : j = i then eqToHom (congrArg Fi hj) ≫ a else gj j hj ≫ b
  refine BinaryCofan.IsColimit.mk (BinaryCofan.mk (f i) k)
    (fun {X} a b => d X a b) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro X a b
    change f i ≫ d X a b = a
    simpa [d] using Cofan.IsColimit.fac hc
      (fun j => if hj : j = i then eqToHom (congrArg Fi hj) ≫ a else gj j hj ≫ b) i
  · intro X a b
    rw [BinaryCofan.mk_inr]
    apply Sheaf.hom_ext
    apply Subfunctor.to_sheafify_lift_unique T
      ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J X.obj).mp X.property)
    ext V x
    have hx : x.1 ∈ T.obj V := x.2
    change x.1 ∈ (⨆ j : {j : I // j ≠ i}, Subfunctor.range (f j.1).hom).obj V at hx
    rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj] at hx
    simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, Subfunctor.range_obj, Set.mem_range] at hx
    obtain ⟨⟨j, hj⟩, y, hy⟩ := hx
    have hmap := congrArg (fun η => η.hom.app V y) (Cofan.IsColimit.fac hc
      (fun j => if hj' : j = i then eqToHom (congrArg Fi hj') ≫ a else gj j hj' ≫ b) j)
    rw [dite_eq_right hj] at hmap
    have hinner : (Subfunctor.homOfLe (T.le_sheafify J)).app V x =
        (gj j hj).hom.app V y := Subtype.ext hy.symm
    change ((k ≫ d X a b).hom.app V) ((Subfunctor.homOfLe (T.le_sheafify J)).app V x) =
      (b.hom.app V) ((Subfunctor.homOfLe (T.le_sheafify J)).app V x)
    rw [hinner]
    calc
      ((k ≫ d X a b).hom.app V) ((gj j hj).hom.app V y)
          = ((gj j hj ≫ k ≫ d X a b).hom.app V) y := rfl
      _ = ((f j ≫ d X a b).hom.app V) y :=
        congrArg (fun z => (d X a b).hom.app V z)
          (congrArg (fun q => q.hom.app V y) (hfacG j hj))
      _ = ((gj j hj ≫ b).hom.app V) y := hmap
      _ = (b.hom.app V) ((gj j hj).hom.app V y) := rfl
  · intro X a b m₀ h1 h2
    -- normalize the spelling of the vertex of the binary cofan, which is `F` only up to
    -- unfolding `BinaryCofan.mk`, so that `≫` and `rw` see a single spelling
    obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m : F ⟶ X, m = m₀ := ⟨m₀, rfl⟩
    have hm1 : f i ≫ m = a := h1
    have hm2 : k ≫ m = b := h2
    change m = d X a b
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hc _ _ fun j => ?_
    by_cases hj : j = i
    · subst j
      calc
        f i ≫ m = a := hm1
        _ = f i ≫ d X a b := by
          simpa [d] using (Cofan.IsColimit.fac hc
            (fun j => if hj' : j = i then eqToHom (congrArg Fi hj') ≫ a
              else gj j hj' ≫ b) i).symm
    · calc
        f j ≫ m = gj j hj ≫ (k ≫ m) := by rw [← hfacG j hj]; simp [Category.assoc]
        _ = gj j hj ≫ b := by rw [hm2]
        _ = f j ≫ d X a b := by
          simpa [d, dite_eq_right hj] using (Cofan.IsColimit.fac hc
            (fun j => if hj' : j = i then eqToHom (congrArg Fi hj') ≫ a
              else gj j hj' ≫ b) j).symm

end General

/-! ### Stacks 0F15 for a coproduct over an arbitrary index type -/

section ArbitraryIndex

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) {I : Type v}
  (Fi : I → Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u))
  (G : Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)) (ι : ∀ i, Fi i ⟶ G)

/-- **Stacks 0F15** for a coproduct over an arbitrary index type: every inclusion of a
summand into a coproduct of sheaves on the big fppf site of `S` is representable by open
immersions. -/
theorem coproductIncl_isOpenImmersion (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk G ι)) (i : I) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@IsOpenImmersion.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) (ι i).hom :=
  coproductInl_isOpenImmersion B S hS (Fi i)
    (coproductComplement (fun j => (ι j).hom) i) G (ι i)
    (coproductComplementIncl (fun j => (ι j).hom) i)
    (isColimit_binaryCofan_coproductComplement ι hc i)

/-- **Stacks 0F15** for a coproduct over an arbitrary index type: every inclusion of a
summand into a coproduct of sheaves on the big fppf site of `S` is representable by closed
immersions. -/
theorem coproductIncl_isClosedImmersion (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk G ι)) (i : I) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@IsClosedImmersion.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) (ι i).hom :=
  coproductInl_isClosedImmersion B S hS (Fi i)
    (coproductComplement (fun j => (ι j).hom) i) G (ι i)
    (coproductComplementIncl (fun j => (ι j).hom) i)
    (isColimit_binaryCofan_coproductComplement ι hc i)

end ArbitraryIndex

/-! ### Stacks 02WP: a summand of a coproduct of algebraic spaces -/

namespace Space

/-- **Stacks 02WP.** Every summand of a sheaf coproduct that is an algebraic space is an
algebraic space. -/
@[stacks 02WP]
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_of_coproduct
    (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (I : Type v)
    (Fᵢ : I → Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u))
    (F : Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u))
    (ι : ∀ i, Fᵢ i ⟶ F)
    (hcoprod : IsColimit (Cofan.mk F ι))
    (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F.obj)
    (i : I) : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (Fᵢ i).obj :=
  isAlgebraicSpace_of_relativelyRepresentable B S hS (ι i).hom
    (coproductInl_isOpenImmersion B S hS (Fᵢ i)
      (otherSheaf (J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (fun j => (ι j).hom) i) F (ι i)
      (otherInclusion (J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (fun j => (ι j).hom) i)
      (splitColimit ι hcoprod i)).1 hF

end Space

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
